text:
maria.c: Quick follow-up from the RFC: I'm proposing we split the inference surface into an 'inference-gateway' (HTTP entry + auth + routing) and 'model-runtime' (batched execution, KV cache). Wanted to capture tradeoffs and a rollout sketch.

jordan: +1 on the split. Main thing I worry about is extra RTT killing p99 for short prompts. Have we measured the cost of an extra hop?

rahul: I ran microbenchmarks yesterday. Extra hop ~0.6-1.2ms within same AZ, but batching mismatch can amplify tail. If we keep batching inside model-runtime and let gateway forward without buffering, p99 impact is manageable.

leo: Important: gateway must not aggregate tokens or delay for batching. Keep it purely routing + auth + ddos/proxy. model-runtime handles batching and KV. That reduces coordination complexity.

maria.c: Agreed. That makes the interface simple: gateway -> stream gRPC to runtime for streaming tokens. We should standardize on a small protobuf for request metadata to avoid exploding headers.

olivia: Also flagging data-plane vs control-plane concerns. We must avoid sending customer PII to control plane. Gateway will be in-customer VPC for Private deployments; need TLS + mTLS between gateway and runtime.

rahul: For Hosted, gateway and runtime will often be co-located. For Dedicated/Private we need clear deployment diagrams. I'll sketch.

maria.c: Proposed minimal proto snippet for the stream:

```proto
message InferenceRequest {
  string request_id = 1;
  repeated bytes prompt_chunks = 2;
  map<string,string> metadata = 3;
}
message InferenceChunk {
  string request_id = 1;
  bytes token = 2;
  bool end_of_stream = 3;
}
service InferenceService {
  rpc StreamInfer(stream InferenceRequest) returns (stream InferenceChunk);
}
```

leo: That looks good. Keep metadata small. Also: include client-side deadline and server-side per-token budget so we can early-abort expensive requests.

jordan: Migration concerns: lots of internal libraries call the current monolith clients. We should implement a compatibility shim that exposes the old client surface but proxies to gateway. That gives time to refactor callers.

olivia: Tech debt paydown: the legacy session store is tangled with auth code. We should extract a thin SessionService (stateless if possible) and back it with a lightweight Redis TTL table. That makes runtime scaling simpler.

maria.c: Rollout plan sketch: 1) implement gateway + runtime prototypes behind feature flag in staging. 2) run replayed production traffic through gateway->runtime with canary routing (10%). 3) validate latency, token cost, and error surface. 4) increase to 50% then full. 5) deprecate monolith routes once all clients move.

rahul: Suggest adding a circuit-breaker on gateway if runtime latency grows, fallback to monolith variant. That keeps SLOs during runtime regressions.

leo: Observability: emit per-request trace id, batching window, batch size, runtime queue time, and per-token exec time. Add a composite metric: tokens_per_ms per model to detect regressions.

maria.c: For testing we should use the perf-replay tool and a synthetic mix that includes short prompts (<32 tokens) and long chat sessions. Need a test harness for KV cache hit/miss to verify correctness.

olivia: Security checklist: mTLS between services, KMS for model keys, RBAC for gateway admin APIs, audit logs for routing changes. For Private, expose an ops endpoint only via VPC.

jordan: One more thing — batching at runtime will change memory footprints. Need automatic admission control: refuse new requests if runtime estimated memory + queued requests > threshold. Don't OOM.

maria.c: Agreed. We'll add an admission controller that tags requests with memory estimate and uses a leaky-bucket limiter.

rahul: On the code side: let's keep the runtime in a separate repo to avoid accidental shared deps and to force clean boundaries. Gateway can depend on runtime proto package only.

maria.c: Action items: rahul to draft deployment diagrams + proto; leo to write observability spec; olivia to enumerate security controls; jordan to prototype shim + canary strategy. I'll consolidate into a short follow-up doc and schedule a 30m sync.

sre-bot: Deploy-checklist created: https://internal.redwood/deploy-checks/inf-split-1769876543 (auto) :white_check_mark:

olivia: tiny question — do we want the gateway to do per-route cost accounting? I'd prefer per-token accounting inside runtime, but gateway can tag tokens with billing metadata.

maria.c: Let's keep billing in runtime (authoritative) and let gateway send tagging hints. That avoids double-counting on retries.

leo: Cool. If nobody objects I'll start the observability doc.

jordan: No objections from me. +1 to separate repos.

maria.c: Thanks everyone. I'll drop the short RFC follow-up in docs and link it here once done. :sparkles:
